OK; I've just spent a couple of days playing this game, and I think I'm about ready to turn in my verdict.
Pros:
- Interesting storyline;
- Decent(ish) combat engine;
- Some downright funny moments.
Cons:
- Opaque combat mechanics (i.e., lack of walkthrough, ingame pedia or other assistance to help understand these numbers getting crunched);
- Zurbaran is USELESS *sadface*;
- The. Baroness. OMG, the Baroness....where to start. The bonus objective is only achieveable if you've looked up where the traps are placed - and that's just to start!
- Siege of Morbal. Nothing ticks one off quite like pushing ahead, winning a tough battle....then, as you're winning, having a rock fall on two characters' heads at once, taking them entirely out of the fight arbitrarily!
- No "RP" in "RPG" - it's a combat grinder, little more. There are hints of an interesting story, but no background, no dialogue, no choices....
Overall, Blackguards feels very, very old-school (think JRPG from the mid-90s, but darker and edgier) - 2014 was better than this! Would not recommend unless on significant discount...

Final Cut combines the storyline and refines the gameplay mechanics of the previous trilogy games.
The gameplay mechanics is improved in all aspects:
1. The character classes are those from the third part of the trilogy, and namely Protector, Bounty Hunter, Elementalist, Umbralist, Phlogistoneer and Constructor;
2. The character attributes are now only 3 and are different for every class, and every attribute is important;
3. The skills are combination from the skills in the trilogy games and are now organized in tiers and branches:
3.1. There are 3 skill-tiers - the first one is accessible from the character creation, the second and the third are accessible at levels 20 and respectively 40;
3.2. The branches are 3 linked skills from each of the tiers, to learn skill from tier 2, you should have learned it's linked skill from tier 1, respectively to learn skill from tier 3, you should have learned it's linked skill from tier 2, and in addition there are synergy-bonuses between the linked skills from given branch, given skill from tier 2 receives synergy from it's linked skill from tier 1, respectively given skill from tier 3 receives synergy from it's linked skills from tier 2 and tier 1;
4. The character progression is now smoother and there is no inflation according to attributes and gear-bonuses;
5. There are now 2 major modes - offline and online:
5.1. In online mode your characters and shared chest is stored on Neocore-cloud and your characters get downloaded for every gaming-session, it requires internet-connectivity but DOESN'T require uninterrupted connection, in this major mode, in addition to the story and multiplayer, the players may experience the new end-game modes (Scenarios, Events and Daily Quests);
5.2. In offline mode your characters and shared chest are stored on your machine, just like it was in the trilogy games, in this major mode you can play story and multiplayer with friends, and the end-game content.
At the end my opinion for the game is that it's really what most of us wanted, it's improved in every aspect. Neocore deserve deep admiration for bringing us the game in this brilliant state. They have it from me!
I was one of the beta-testers of the game, and I am grateful to the devs that they gave me the chance to contribute somehow to this brilliant game!

Quake III Arena is an awesome fast-paced arena-styled multiplayer FPS game. A pure deathmatch game at it's best. The controls are perfect, the vanilla graphics are still good today, and the gameplay... ♥♥♥♥ing awesome! One of my favorite features is the ability to play against bots with friends. Very fun if you just want to co-op in the game.
I will say one thing. This game will test your skills and even help you improve your aim and reaction time as the combat is fast and fierce. After playing this game, I can say I am better at FPS games, especially ones with rocket launchers ;). This is one thing I cannot say you will get from most FPS games. This gives it another reason why this game kicks so much a$$! Not only are you having fun, but you are excersising your hand-to-eye coordination.
This game is also very easy to mod. All you need to do is open the .pk3 files in a program like WinZip or WinRar and you can replace the game's sound effects, graphics, and models with custom ones you either downloaded or made yourself.
Talking about mods, I highly recommend downloading ioQuake3 (
). It replaces Quake 3's rendering engine to suit modern machines giving you better net code and the ability to match your computer's native resolution. You can also download other mods for ioQuake3 to improve the game. Some other mods I recommend is the high res texture pack (
) and the Metal-Tech v2.0 mod that replaces the textures for the weapons with higher res ones (
).
On final note, this game is pure awesomeness and has a high replay value. If you are interested in playing a fast-paced FPS game to test out or improve upon your twitch skills, this is the game for you!

