It's been a long time since I've been so happy to just discover things about a game. going in with no expectations I was pleasantly surprised at every turn. I can't lie however and say this game is perfect. It's the space exploration game I've wanted for a long time. to play the game and enjoy it I suggest having at least one friend play it with you. many of the ships require more than one person to keep flying it and mining less tedious. this game is extremely large but as of right now it's missing quite a bit of depth and becoming bored is understandable as an experience I've loved what I've experienced so far, but this game is extremely tedious, sometimes tedious to the point of not being fun. the resource gathering is fun and interesting for maybe an hour if you're patient but if you want to stary with a somewhat large ship you'll have some trouble gathering the things you'll need. (There are ways to negate this but...) and once you have your ship and you've mined away from the starting space station, maybe traveled too another solar system it dosesn't seem like there's a whole lot to do. I might be missing something but neither my friends nor I could figure out what was next. I'll chalk that up to it being early accesses of course. and I can't wait to see the direction this game takes!
TL;DR: good game, extremely tedious sometimes for what seems like no reason. can't wait for an update.

Great dev team: Always progressing at a good pace, even if on details the casual player does not notice, they do "churn" out a impressive amount of work. Their communication only disappoints the ones that don't bother to read what is posted or announced. Dev team plays the game also, won't be rare to see them playing once the EA workload normalises;
Complex craft system made simple: seems to not make sense, right?  Until you try it. Does require collecting recipes but if everything was too easy, wouldn't make it enjoyable in my opinion;
Combat system: even in a Alpha state one can feel the variety that will soon be introduced with new animations and mechanics. Is rather enjoyable as it is currently and the approach that no player is beyond the reach of a low level is intersting to say the least. Does require habituation and knowledge of the fight mechanics, of course, but easy to learn once you try;
Open world: full of nooks and crannies, a apparently small Alpha map (check the planned final map and be amazed when compared) will keep you busy and roaming around for months. Always something you did not notice even when you went by that place dozens of times;
Community: despite the recent EA, the community binds together after a bit of getting used to the game. Helping new players seems something that occurs naturally once a former new player has "soaked in" what the older players know. There are minor issues that are (part of a Alpha) simply solved by constant sharing of workarounds and fixes.
Overall: a bit of everything for everyone, lots to find out and figure out. Addictive and fun =)
